<title>USA: D&amp;P rates Bank International Indonesia.</title>
<headline>D&amp;P rates Bank International Indonesia.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-04-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Duff &amp; Phelps Credit Rating Co said Monday it assigned a Triple B credit rating to the long-term senior unsecured debt of Bank International Indonesia.</p>
<p>The rating applies to both foreign currency and local currency debt. At the end of 1996, its assets totaled US$7.5 billion.</p>
<p>Bank International Indonesia is majority owned by the Sinar Mas Group, Indonesia's second-largest conglomerate.</p>
<p>Duff &amp; Phelps said the rating reflects the bank's track record of above industry average profitability, solid asset quality and favorable market position.</p>
<p>	 ((Reuters Chicago Newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
